d an email to their general mailbox : XXXXXXXXXXXX or something along those lines. Meanwhile, the lender kept sending me letters saying how they wanted to work with me. They also kept sending me offers to refinance my mortgage and HELOC. They even sent an appraiser, unsolicited and unwarranted to inspect my property. When the appraiser showed up, he wanted access to the house. When I refused he told me that he would go back to Chase and start eviction proceedings. When I asked why, he said that if he did not get access, it meant that I was not paying my mortgage. When I explained to him that not a single payment was late in the last 3 years, he said that its not his problem and that this is a standard process. After the closing, when the loan was finally paid off, someone from Chase called me to ask me if I 'd ever do business with them again and that they had great programs for the new property I purchase. He said all I would have to do is fill out a credit app over the phone. When I asked for his name and department, he hung up. When I called their privacy team to add my name to the "" do not contact list '' they refused and told me to simply disregard the offers they were sending if I was not interested. 
